    "paragraph": "A prospective correlational study evaluated the Theory of Planned Behaviour's ability to forecast parent-child joint walking frequency across school, non-school, and leisure trips using online surveys administered one month apart to 128 parents in Scotland. Synthetic simulations across eight data-generating processes and two empirical datasets in Dublin and Kola were used to evaluate leave-one-out cross-validation for bandwidth selection in geographically weighted principal component analysis. Additionally, a survey of 100 neighborhood food businesses in Medellín, Colombia, combined with a contextual documentary review, evaluated how small enterprises adopt digital technologies and generate community value.",
